{"index":1188,"node_id":"2f605ac0-e168-45b0-a135-c5bfbaf7e037","parent":"020aecb2-3eb9-4146-baa6-552d791152bb","role":"assistant","author_name":null,"create_time":1791085358.893327,"update_time":1791085366.692928,"content_type":"text","status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":true,"recipient":"all","model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","default_model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","part":1,"parts_total":1,"text":"They were GitHub connector calls for the one rename.\n\n- **`fetch_file`** — read the current JSON and obtain its blob SHA, which GitHub requires for an in-place update.\n- **`update_file`** — replace `truth_table` with `truthtable`.\n- **`list_resources`** — load the available GitHub action schema.\n- **branch/ref fetch + `create_blob` attempt** — fallback attempts after the first `update_file` call was blocked by the connector. Those attempts were unnecessary in the final result and made no repository change.\n- **final `fetch_file`** — verify the committed file actually contained `truthtable`.\n\nSo the only meaningful repository mutation was the successful `update_file` commit. The extra calls were connector-handling overhead, not additional work on your project."}
